A||||11||My7Fieros||Just got back from The Fiero Factory!||||14||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||11-09-2001||12:31 AM||||....and what a cool place it is! After struggling on and off for over a year w/ an 87 GT Ive got w/idle probs (bad, and some other minor mechanical probs), I finally threw in the towel and decided to send her to the pros!<BR>So me, my g/f, and a friend of mine took his Yukon, rented an auto transport from U-Haul, loaded the Fiero up, and made the (roughly) 3 hour pilgrimage to Huntsville, AL to the Fiero Factory. I told the mechanics there about the probs it had and they were like "ok, no biggie". Keep in mind these people do this everyday, for a living, so this problem Im sure seemed trivial. I walked around throughout the place, drooling of course, and signed my name (rather largely to I might add   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) to the "Hall of Fame Wall". There were sooo many sigs on there...and Im sure lots of forum members, but since I know most of you buy your username and not your real name, I really couldnt tell whos who. I did see Moo Cow's sig on the wall.<BR>The lot outside is full of Fieros...most in rough shape, but still fun to look at none the less. Unfortunantly, Ed Parks wasnt there..he was on his way back from Dallas. But Rosie and another Ed and the mechanics were there, as well as Ed's (the other Ed) blue Cadillac powered "Taz" Fiero. My god does that thing sound good! A <I>bit</I> guady for my taste, but still pretty nice none the less. Im gonna go back and pick it up whens its finished...no rush. <BR>I highly recommend going there...its a MUST for the true Fiero enthusiasts!<BR>BTW sorry, I didnt take a camera.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||GTFiero1||11-09-2001||01:53 AM||||yay, im the firt to reply and i will have to say that i<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
