Z||000009||cadero2dmax||11-10-2001||01:19 PM||||I would recommend that everybody make plans to attend his Swap Meet there the last weekend in April - - you could even meet some of the "Fiero Famous", Paul McGibbon, Rodney Dickman, Darrel (can't think of his last name, but he markets hubs for GA conversions, and strut tower braces), Dave Held, Kevin Leslie (Design One). Even that guy that has the rep for racin' Fieros - had a multi-colored racer on display the year before last - I think his name is George Ryan - will be there too. This year I will have the Challenge Fiero and my SE there. <P>I would highly recommend if you want to meet at least a couple hundred other Fiero nuts, some of whom you have been corresponding or buying products from, come on down!! This is where a lot of the vendors demo new products - I have hard that this is whre Held Motorsports will release their new tubular cradle for stock bodied Fieros!!<P><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>86 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||10
